# `π` to 32 decimals

Mathlib proves `π` to 20 decimals (`Real.pi_gt_d20`, `Real.pi_lt_d20`). The
Cody–Waite reduction in `kernel_fast` subtracts `N (p1 + p2 + p3)`, which
differs from `N π` by `|N| · 1.7·10^-31`; bounding that needs `π` to about 32
decimals. The witnesses below are checked by Mathlib's own `pi_lower_bound` /
`pi_upper_bound` tactics; they were generated by `lean/pi_witness.py`, a port
of the Mathematica script documented in `Mathlib/Analysis/Real/Pi/Bounds.lean`.
-/

